# REP prints the last printed character again, as many times as its
# count says, where an omitted or zero count means 1. The copies take the
# path printed text takes, so they wrap and scroll. REP repeats the last
# character even after a carriage return and a line feed, and each copy
# takes the pen in force when REP runs.
# spec: ctlseqs, REP ("Repeat the preceding graphic character Ps times"); ECMA-48 8.3.103 REP
# covers: text.rep
size 10 4
send "ab\e[3b"
dump state
send "\r\nx\e[b"
dump state
send "\r\nyz\e[0b"
dump state
send "\r\n\e[3b"
dump state
send "q\e[99b"
dump state
send "\e[4;9H\e[1;31mR\e[m\e[5b"
dump state
